# Deep felt-experience: atypical and novel synthetic opioids.
from gen import D
F={}
def S(k,o,p,pl,c): F[k]={"onset":o,"peak":p,"plateau":pl,"comedown":c}
S("tianeptine",
["Tianeptine is an antidepressant sold by prescription in parts of Europe and Asia, and in the US it has been sold at gas stations under names like 'Tianaa' and 'ZaZa' despite FDA warnings. At much more than medical amounts it acts as a full mu-opioid agonist. Swallowed, it comes on fast: a warm, buzzing lift in the chest, a loosening of the body and a sudden easing of anxiety.","Mentally the onset is often described as bright and stimulating more than sleepy: a burst of contentment, sociability and confidence, sometimes compared to a short hydrocodone high with an antidepressant glow.","It is very short-acting, so the onset is already the start of the decline, which is why people who misuse it often take it many times a day."],
["At its peak the body feels warm and light, with mild itching, sweating, narrowed pupils and sometimes nausea. At higher amounts heaviness and nodding take over.","Mentally the peak is a clean-feeling euphoria and calm; worries vanish and people feel chatty and upbeat. As amounts rise, it becomes dreamier and more sedated.","Overdose with slowed breathing, confusion, agitation and heart problems has been reported, often with other drugs. Naloxone reverses the opioid part."],
["The plateau is short, often under two hours. The warmth thins into a mild relaxed buzz while sweating and dry mouth continue.","Mentally the brightness fades quickly into restlessness and a desire for more; people often watch the clock for the next dose.","This rapid cycle drives heavy, compulsive use and quick tolerance."],
["The comedown is fast and unpleasant: aches, yawning, goosebumps, sweating and a crawling discomfort in the legs.","Emotionally people describe sharp anxiety, irritability and low mood, sometimes worse than with classic opioids because the antidepressant lift also disappears.","Withdrawal from heavy daily use can be severe, with insomnia, agitation, diarrhea and intense craving, and has sometimes needed hospital care. Medical help with tapering or buprenorphine is recommended."])
S("7-hydroxymitragynine",
["7-hydroxymitragynine (7-OH) is a kratom alkaloid that is much stronger than kratom leaf itself and is now sold in concentrated tablets and shots at smoke shops. Swallowed, it comes on over a short time with a warm, heavy loosening through the body and a fast drop in aches.","Mentally the onset is far more opioid-like than kratom leaf: a deep, comfortable calm and euphoria, with little of the stimulant edge that low-amount kratom gives.","Because products vary widely in strength and labeling, people can get far more than they expect, and tolerance builds quickly."],
["At its peak the body feels heavy, warm and itchy, with pinpoint pupils, slowed breathing, nausea and nodding.","Mentally the peak is a dreamy, sedated contentment much like a prescription opioid.","Overdose and deaths have been reported, especially with other sedatives. Naloxone reverses it."],
["The plateau lasts a few hours of drowsy warmth, constipation and dry mouth, the body pinned in a relaxed heaviness.","Mentally people feel quiet, slow and inward, with poor focus and slowed reactions.","Breathing suppression continues, and stacking more doses during the plateau is a common path to overdose."],
["The comedown brings tiredness, aching and restlessness, sometimes with a runny nose and yawning.","Emotionally people often feel flat, anxious and craving, more sharply than with plain kratom.","Daily use leads to opioid dependence; withdrawal is like other opioids and buprenorphine treatment can help."])
S("mgm-15",
["MGM-15 is a semi-synthetic kratom-derived opioid sold online in recent years as a very strong product, related to mitragynine pseudoindoxyl. Little research exists. Users describe a fast-building opioid warmth and heaviness.","Mentally the onset is reported as a strong, smooth calm and euphoria.","Its potency relative to kratom is high and products are unregulated, so the margin for error is narrow."],
["At its peak the body is heavy and sedated, with itching and slowed breathing.","Mentally the peak is dreamlike and detached.","Overdose risk is real, especially combined with alcohol or benzodiazepines; naloxone is expected to work."],
["The plateau is reported as long, several hours of sedation and constipation.","Mentally people feel slow and drowsy.","Breathing remains suppressed throughout."],
["The comedown brings aches, restlessness and fatigue.","Emotionally low mood and craving.","Dependence develops quickly; withdrawal resembles strong opioids."])
S("akuamma",
["Akuamma seeds, from a West African tree, contain alkaloids that act weakly on opioid receptors. Swallowed, the onset is mild and gradual: a faint relaxation, slight easing of aches and sometimes nausea from the very bitter seeds.","Mentally most people notice only subtle calm, if anything; a few describe mild mood lift or sleepiness.","Effects vary greatly, and research on safety is limited."],
["At its peak the body may feel slightly heavy and relaxed, with dizziness or stomach upset.","Mentally the state is quiet and calm, far milder than kratom or prescription opioids.","Mixing with other sedatives or opioids adds unknown risk."],
["The plateau is a few hours of mild relaxation.","Mentally faintly calm.","Nausea may persist."],
["The comedown is usually mild tiredness.","Emotionally little change.","Dependence is not well studied."])
S("loperamide",
["Loperamide (Imodium) is an anti-diarrhea opioid that normally stays in the gut because the body pumps it out of the brain. At ordinary use there is no mental effect: just a calmer, slower bowel.","Some people take enormous amounts to ease withdrawal or seek a high; at those levels a little reaches the brain, giving a faint calm and easing of withdrawal aches rather than a real euphoria.","That misuse is dangerous because loperamide at such amounts disrupts the heart's electrical rhythm."],
["At very high misuse amounts, the body feels mildly heavy and severely constipated, but the main event is the heart: palpitations, fainting, irregular rhythms and sometimes cardiac arrest.","Mentally there is mild sedation and relief from withdrawal, but little pleasure.","Deaths have occurred from heart rhythm problems. Naloxone helps breathing but not the heart effects; emergency care is needed for fainting or palpitations."],
["The plateau is long because loperamide clears slowly at high levels, with continued constipation and heart strain.","Mentally people feel dull and tired.","Heart rhythm danger can persist for days."],
["The comedown brings withdrawal symptoms back, along with abdominal discomfort.","Emotionally anxious and low.","Anyone using loperamide to manage withdrawal should seek proper treatment such as buprenorphine or methadone instead."])
S("salvinorin-kappa",
["Salvinorin A, from the plant Salvia divinorum, is a powerful kappa-opioid agonist, unlike the mu-opioids people usually mean by 'opioid'. Its onset is extremely fast and disorienting, a sudden shift in reality rather than warmth.","Mentally the onset can feel like being pulled, peeled or folded out of the normal world, often with loss of awareness of the body and room.","It gives no opioid comfort, and naloxone does not reliably reverse it. See the salvia page for its full experience."],
["At its peak the body may feel heavy, twisted or absent, and people may move or stumble without awareness.","Mentally the peak is overwhelming dissociation and dreamlike or bizarre visions; many find it frightening.","The main risks are falls and injury, so a sober sitter is essential."],
["The plateau is short, minutes rather than hours.","Mentally reality reassembles in pieces, often confusing.","Lingering disorientation may remain briefly."],
["The comedown is quick, with tiredness or a strange afterglow.","Emotionally people may feel shaken or reflective.","It has low addiction potential but can be distressing."])
S("u-47700",
["U-47700 ('pink') is a synthetic opioid developed by Upjohn in the 1970s that resurfaced as a research chemical around 2015, causing many deaths. Its onset is fast: a warm rush, heavy limbs and strong relief.","Mentally people describe a short, intense euphoria similar to a strong prescription opioid.","Powders and counterfeit pills containing it vary unpredictably in strength."],
["At its peak the body is heavy and itchy, pupils pinpoint and breathing markedly slowed.","Mentally dreamy contentment and nodding.","Fatal overdoses, often with other drugs, led to worldwide bans. Naloxone works but may need repeating."],
["The plateau is short, encouraging redosing and stacking.","Mentally the calm fades into restlessness.","Breathing risk rises with every extra dose."],
["The comedown is fast, with aches, sweating and craving.","Emotionally anxious and low.","Dependence develops quickly."])
S("ah-7921",
["AH-7921 is a synthetic opioid from the 1970s sold as a research chemical in the 2010s. Its onset brings warmth, relaxation and strong pain relief.","Mentally a calm, mildly euphoric detachment.","Purity and strength of research samples are unknown."],
["At its peak heavy sedation and slowed breathing.","Mentally dreamy contentment.","Several deaths led to international control."],
["The plateau is a few hours of sedation.","Mentally slow and foggy.","Breathing remains suppressed."],
["The comedown brings aches and restlessness.","Emotionally low.","Dependence develops with repeated use."])
S("mt-45",
["MT-45 is a synthetic opioid unrelated to fentanyl that was sold online around 2013 to 2014. Its onset brings warmth and sedation, sometimes with a dissociative feeling.","Mentally people described calm detachment.","It was linked to unusual harms: hearing loss, skin lesions, hair loss and nail problems."],
["At its peak heavy sedation and slowed breathing.","Mentally foggy and dreamlike.","Deaths occurred, often with other drugs."],
["The plateau lasted a few hours.","Mentally slow and detached.","Breathing stays suppressed."],
["The comedown brought aches and fatigue.","Emotionally low.","Long-term harms to hearing and skin could persist."])
S("etorphine",
["Etorphine (M99) is used to immobilize large animals like elephants and is thousands of times stronger than morphine. Accidental human exposure through a needle stick or splash brings almost immediate heaviness, dizziness and breathing problems.","Mentally there is rapid drowsiness and confusion.","Veterinarians carry its reversal drug, diprenorphine or naloxone, because exposure can be fatal within minutes."],
["At its peak, breathing slows or stops, blood pressure drops and the person collapses.","Mentally unconsciousness follows quickly.","This is an extreme medical emergency."],
["Without reversal, sedation is deep and prolonged.","Mentally no awareness.","Repeated naloxone and hospital care are needed."],
["After reversal, people feel shaky, nauseated and exhausted.","Emotionally frightened.","It has no recreational role."])
S("fentanyl-analogs",
["Fentanyl analogs such as acetylfentanyl, furanylfentanyl and carfentanil appear in street powders and counterfeit pills. Their onset is very fast: an intense wave of warmth and heaviness.","Mentally a sudden, strong euphoria and calm, often shorter than heroin's.","Their potencies vary enormously, and buyers usually do not know which analog they have."],
["At its peak the body is heavy, breathing slows dramatically, and chest rigidity can appear.","Mentally dreamy then sedated.","Overdose can come within minutes; repeated naloxone may be needed."],
["The plateau is short, driving frequent use.","Mentally the calm fades fast.","Each new dose is a fresh overdose risk."],
["The comedown is quick and harsh: aches, sweats and intense craving.","Emotionally anxious and desperate.","Dependence is severe; treatment with buprenorphine or methadone saves lives."])
S("brorphine",
["Brorphine is a synthetic opioid that appeared in the US drug supply in 2019 to 2020, often mixed with heroin or fentanyl. Its onset brings warmth, heaviness and relief.","Mentally a calm euphoria similar to fentanyl.","It is often unknowingly consumed."],
["At its peak heavy sedation and slowed breathing.","Mentally dreamy.","Deaths have occurred; naloxone works."],
["The plateau is a few hours.","Mentally slow.","Breathing stays suppressed."],
["The comedown brings aches and craving.","Emotionally low.","Dependence like other strong opioids."])
for k,v in F.items():
    if k in D: D[k]["feel"]=v
